Sure.

786
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:31,840
I work for Greencore Manufacturing.

787
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:34,440
We operate in the renewable energy industry.

788
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:38,460
We're a mid-sized company with around 250 employees.

789
00:41:38,460 --> 00:41:43,120
Our main focus is producing solar panels for residential and commercial clients.

790
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:47,840
One of our key strengths is our commitment to sustainability and innovation.

791
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:50,320
That sounds very professional and complete.

792
00:41:50,320 --> 00:41:52,520
And notice that it flows naturally.

793
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:55,080
It doesn't sound memorized or robotic.

794
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:58,160
I like that you use the phrase, we operate in.

795
00:41:58,160 --> 00:42:01,000
That sounds more formal than just saying we are in.

796
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:04,960
Yes, operate in is very common in business English.

797
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:07,600
What are some other useful phrases people can use?

798
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:12,680
You can say, we specialize in, we focus on, we provide,

799
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:14,880
we offer, we deliver.

800
00:42:14,880 --> 00:42:18,520
Let's explain the difference between provide and offer.

801
00:42:18,520 --> 00:42:20,080
Good question, they're similar,

802
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:22,720
but provide sounds slightly more formal.

803
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:26,760
For example, we provide financial consulting services.

804
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:30,160
And offer sounds slightly more customer focused?

805
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:35,240
Yes, for example, we offer customized solutions to small businesses.

806
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:37,720
Let's talk about describing company size.

807
00:42:37,720 --> 00:42:39,760
How can someone do that naturally?

808
00:42:39,760 --> 00:42:45,660
You can say, we're a small startup with about 20 employees, or we're a large multinational

809
00:42:45,660 --> 00:42:49,720
corporation with offices in over 30 countries.

810
00:42:49,720 --> 00:42:53,400
Multinational corporation means a company that operates in many countries.

811
00:42:53,400 --> 00:42:56,040
Exactly, that's strong vocabulary.

812
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:58,440
What about describing company culture?

813
00:42:58,440 --> 00:43:00,620
That's something many people are asked about.

814
00:43:00,620 --> 00:43:03,720
Yes, especially in interviews or networking events.

815
00:43:03,720 --> 00:43:08,800
You could say, we have a collaborative and fast-paced work environment, or our company

816
00:43:08,800 --> 00:43:13,600
culture values innovation, teamwork, and continuous improvement.

817
00:43:13,600 --> 00:43:17,440
Fast-paced means the work environment is busy and dynamic.

818
00:43:17,440 --> 00:43:18,440
Correct.

819
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:21,080
Now let's imagine a networking situation.

820
00:43:21,080 --> 00:43:24,540
Someone at a conference asks, so, what does your company do?

821
00:43:24,540 --> 00:43:26,020
How would you respond?

822
00:43:26,020 --> 00:43:30,140
In a networking context, your answer should be shorter and more engaging.

823
00:43:30,140 --> 00:43:34,940
For example, we're a digital marketing agency that helps brands grow their online presence

824
00:43:34,940 --> 00:43:37,340
through data-driven strategies.

825
00:43:37,340 --> 00:43:39,220
That's clear and impactful.

826
00:43:39,220 --> 00:43:42,380
And if they're interested, they'll ask follow-up questions.

827
00:43:42,380 --> 00:43:45,180
Let's talk about describing your company's mission.

828
00:43:45,180 --> 00:43:47,500
That's very common in business conversations.

829
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:52,660
Yes, you could say, our mission is to make technology accessible and affordable for

830
00:43:52,660 --> 00:43:53,660
everyone.

831
00:43:53,660 --> 00:43:58,140
we aim to improve health care outcomes through innovative medical devices.

832
00:43:58,140 --> 00:44:01,740
I like the phrase, we aim to. It sounds purposeful.

833
00:44:01,740 --> 00:44:04,540
It does. It shows direction and vision.

834
00:44:04,540 --> 00:44:07,260
What about describing clients or customers?

835
00:44:07,260 --> 00:44:11,980
You can say, our clients include small and medium-sized enterprises,

836
00:44:11,980 --> 00:44:15,740
or we primarily serve corporate clients in the finance sector.

837
00:44:16,300 --> 00:44:21,420
Small and medium-sized enterprises, that's often abbreviated as SMEs.

838
00:44:21,420 --> 00:44:27,020
Yes, exactly. Let's do a role play. I'll ask you about your company. Great, go ahead.

839
00:44:27,580 --> 00:44:32,380
Can you tell me a bit about your company? Sure, I work for Nova Logistics,

840
00:44:32,380 --> 00:44:36,940
we're a global supply chain management company. We specialize in transportation and

841
00:44:36,940 --> 00:44:42,540
warehousing solutions for international retailers. We have over a thousand employees worldwide and

842
00:44:42,540 --> 00:44:48,300
operate in more than 15 countries. That's very clear. Now I'll answer. Ask me the question.

843
00:44:48,300 --> 00:44:50,300
What does your company do?

844
00:44:50,300 --> 00:44:52,300
I work for Brightwave Consulting.

845
00:44:52,300 --> 00:44:54,300
We're a boutique consulting firm

846
00:44:54,300 --> 00:44:56,300
focusing on business transformation

847
00:44:56,300 --> 00:44:58,300
and process optimization.

848
00:44:58,300 --> 00:45:00,300
We mainly work with mid-sized companies

849
00:45:00,300 --> 00:45:02,300
looking to improve efficiency

850
00:45:02,300 --> 00:45:04,300
and reduce operational costs.

851
00:45:04,300 --> 00:45:05,300
Excellent.

852
00:45:05,300 --> 00:45:07,300
Boutique Firms suggests it's smaller

853
00:45:07,300 --> 00:45:09,300
and more specialized.

854
00:45:09,300 --> 00:45:12,300
Yes, it implies a personalized service.

855
00:45:12,300 --> 00:45:14,300
Let's talk about achievements.

856
00:45:14,300 --> 00:45:17,300
Sometimes you may want to highlight your company's success.

857
00:45:17,300 --> 00:45:23,300
Yes, especially in sales meetings. You could say, we've recently expanded into the Asian market,

858
00:45:23,300 --> 00:45:27,460
or we were recognized as one of the top employers in our industry last year.

859
00:45:28,020 --> 00:45:34,020
That adds credibility. Exactly. What about describing company structure? You could say,

860
00:45:34,020 --> 00:45:38,980
we're organized into several departments, including sales, marketing, operations,

861
00:45:38,980 --> 00:45:45,540
and customer support. Organized into means divided into. Correct. Now let's discuss

862
00:45:45,540 --> 00:45:51,060
common mistakes, what should people avoid when talking about their company? Avoid speaking to

863
00:45:51,060 --> 00:45:59,140
generally. For example, saying, we do many things is too vague. Vague means unclear. Yes, be specific.

864
00:45:59,140 --> 00:46:03,940
Also, avoid using too much technical jargon if your listener is not familiar with your industry.

865
00:46:04,580 --> 00:46:10,580
Jargon means specialized language. Exactly. Use clear and simple explanations.

866
00:46:10,580 --> 00:46:17,220
Let's review useful vocabulary from today. Industry, the business sector, operate to conduct

867
00:46:17,220 --> 00:46:24,180
business activities, specialize to focus on a particular area, multi-national operating in

868
00:46:24,180 --> 00:46:30,420
multiple countries, mission, the company's purpose or goal, client, a customer who receives

869
00:46:30,420 --> 00:46:36,500
professional services, innovation, introducing new ideas or products. Before we finish,

870
00:46:36,500 --> 00:46:41,380
Let's summarize. When talking about your company, start with the name in industry.

871
00:46:41,940 --> 00:46:47,060
Mention size and location if relevant. Explain products or services clearly.

872
00:46:47,620 --> 00:46:53,780
Highlight strengths or achievements if appropriate. And adjust the length depending on the situation.

873
00:46:53,780 --> 00:46:58,580
Now it's time for our question of the day. How would you describe your company in English?

874
00:46:59,220 --> 00:47:04,500
Write a short description using phrases like we specialize in or we operate in.

875
00:47:04,500 --> 00:47:11,140
in. Practice saying it out loud until it sounds natural. Thank you so much for joining us today.

876
00:47:11,140 --> 00:47:15,540
Keep practicing, stay confident, and keep improving your business English. We'll see

877
00:47:15,540 --> 00:47:19,440
you in the next episode. Goodbye and take care.

878
00:47:19,440 --> 00:47:22,320
Hello and welcome to Business English Conversations.

879
00:47:22,320 --> 00:47:25,640
Hi, everyone. We're very happy you're here with us today.

880
00:47:25,640 --> 00:47:26,840
I'm Erica.

881
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:28,040
