1047
00:53:45,180 --> 00:53:46,380
Good scenario.

1048
00:53:46,380 --> 00:53:47,540
Possible answers.

1049
00:53:47,540 --> 00:53:50,100
We've been in business for over 10 years.

1050
00:53:50,100 --> 00:53:53,780
were a relatively new company founded in 2023.

1051
00:53:53,780 --> 00:53:56,540
We've been operating for more than two decades.

1052
00:53:56,540 --> 00:53:59,140
Example, we're a well-established firm

1053
00:53:59,140 --> 00:54:01,500
with 25 years of experience.

1054
00:54:01,500 --> 00:54:02,860
Very polished.

1055
00:54:02,860 --> 00:54:05,460
Let's discuss describing market position.

1056
00:54:05,460 --> 00:54:06,800
Interesting topic.

1057
00:54:06,800 --> 00:54:09,180
You might hear we're a market leader.

1058
00:54:09,180 --> 00:54:12,380
We're one of the fastest growing companies in our sector.

1059
00:54:12,380 --> 00:54:14,020
We're a niche provider.

1060
00:54:14,020 --> 00:54:16,460
We're an emerging player in the industry.

1061
00:54:16,460 --> 00:54:17,780
Let's try examples.

1062
00:54:17,780 --> 00:54:21,820
We're considered a leading provider of cloud security solutions.

1063
00:54:21,820 --> 00:54:26,020
We're a niche consultancy focusing on sustainability strategies.

1064
00:54:26,020 --> 00:54:26,820
Excellent.

1065
00:54:26,820 --> 00:54:29,500
Let's talk about keeping explanations simple.

1066
00:54:29,500 --> 00:54:31,500
Very important for clarity.

1067
00:54:31,500 --> 00:54:34,220
Especially when speaking with non-specialists.

1068
00:54:34,220 --> 00:54:36,060
Or international partners.

1069
00:54:36,060 --> 00:54:39,420
Example, we help companies improve efficiency.

1070
00:54:39,420 --> 00:54:42,060
We design and produce office furniture.

1071
00:54:42,060 --> 00:54:44,740
We provide online education services.

1072
00:54:44,740 --> 00:54:47,300
Simple language can be very powerful.

1073
00:54:47,300 --> 00:54:49,160
Clarity over complexity.

1074
00:54:49,160 --> 00:54:52,480
Let's role play a casual professional conversation.

1075
00:54:52,480 --> 00:54:53,320
Okay.

1076
00:54:53,320 --> 00:54:55,040
So what does your company do?

1077
00:54:55,040 --> 00:54:57,100
We're a digital marketing agency.

1078
00:54:57,100 --> 00:54:59,320
We help brands grow their online presence

1079
00:54:59,320 --> 00:55:01,640
through social media, content strategy,

1080
00:55:01,640 --> 00:55:03,120
and paid advertising.

1081
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:04,560
That sounds interesting.

1082
00:55:04,560 --> 00:55:06,120
Who do you usually work with?

1083
00:55:06,120 --> 00:55:08,440
Mostly startups and small businesses.

1084
00:55:08,440 --> 00:55:10,160
Very natural flow.

1085
00:55:10,160 --> 00:55:12,600
Let's role play a more formal situation.

1086
00:55:12,600 --> 00:55:15,520
Client meeting, could you tell us about your company?

1087
00:55:15,520 --> 00:55:21,520
Certainly. We're a financial consulting firm specializing in risk management and investment strategy.

1088
00:55:21,520 --> 00:55:24,020
We work with corporate clients across Europe.

1089
00:55:24,020 --> 00:55:28,020
Polished and professional. Let's discuss confidence again.

1090
00:55:28,020 --> 00:55:29,520
Always relevant.

1091
00:55:29,520 --> 00:55:33,020
When talking about your company, speak clearly and positively.

1092
00:55:33,020 --> 00:55:35,020
Avoid sounding uncertain.

1093
00:55:35,020 --> 00:55:39,520
Instead of, uh, we kind of do different things.

1094
00:55:39,520 --> 00:55:41,520
Say, we provide.

1095
00:55:41,520 --> 00:55:43,020
We specialize in.

1096
00:55:43,020 --> 00:55:44,020
We focus on.

1097
00:55:44,020 --> 00:55:47,020
Strong verbs create strong impressions.

1098
00:55:47,020 --> 00:55:49,020
Let's talk about enthusiasm.

1099
00:55:49,020 --> 00:55:51,020
Yes, energy matters.

1100
00:55:51,020 --> 00:55:53,020
But balance is key.

1101
00:55:53,020 --> 00:55:55,020
Professional enthusiasm.

1102
00:55:55,020 --> 00:55:58,020
Example, we're really excited about our new product line.

1103
00:55:58,020 --> 00:56:01,020
We're proud of our customer-centric approach.

1104
00:56:01,020 --> 00:56:03,020
We're passionate about innovation.

1105
00:56:03,020 --> 00:56:04,020
Very natural.

1106
00:56:04,020 --> 00:56:07,020
So what's the key message of today's conversation?

1107
00:56:07,020 --> 00:56:11,020
Talking about your company should be clear, concise, and confident.

1108
00:56:11,020 --> 00:56:13,020
Explain what the company does.

1109
00:56:13,020 --> 00:56:18,920
mention industry or specialization, add clients size or strengths if relevant,

1110
00:56:18,920 --> 00:56:25,140
and keep it natural. Not memorized, not overly complicated. That brings us to the

1111
00:56:25,140 --> 00:56:28,940
end of today's episode. We hope this conversation helps you describe your

1112
00:56:28,940 --> 00:56:33,340
company more confidently in English. Before we go, here's a small practice

1113
00:56:33,340 --> 00:56:37,900
idea. Try describing your company out loud. Imagine you're at a networking

1114
00:56:37,900 --> 00:56:43,580
event or in an interview. Practice builds fluency and fluency builds confidence.

1115
00:56:43,580 --> 00:56:48,100
Thank you so much for listening to Business English Conversations. See you

1116
00:56:48,100 --> 00:56:52,620
in the next episode. Goodbye. Bye everyone.
